  "description": "<p>The Australia Institute of Business and Technology is one of Australiaâ€™s top private vocational education providers. Founded in 2015, the institute has recruited over 10,000 international students from over 80 different countries around the world.</p><p>Modern campuses are situated in Brisbane, Sydney and Hobart, with AIBT-accredited courses offering the same nationally recognised qualifications available through TAFE.</p><h2>What is the acceptance rate for Australia Institute of Business and Technology?</h2><p>The acceptance rate for the Australia Institute of Business and Technology is 90%.</p> <p>AIBT offers the practical experience of simulated labs, training restaurants and engineering workshops to help students gain invaluable employable skills aligned with current industry standards. The high-tech virtual classrooms allow online students to attend real-time/recorded classes anywhere globally. AIBT is well-funded, so students can use the latest software and hardware available. The library at AIBT houses an extensive collection of books, journals, and online resources and an impressive structure. Student lounges and relaxing common areas are provided in addition to food places for students to rest and recharge.</p><p>Australia is a popular international destination for several reasons. The sunny weather and go-getter lifestyle provide diverse opportunities for recreational enjoyment and gainful employment. Whether students are based in Brisbane, Sydney or Hobart, the beach and drinking culture rivals other global destinations, with nightlife opportunities that will expand student horizons. Healthy food choices, restaurants and tourist attractions are also plentiful in these areas.</p> <p><strong>Student Life</strong></p> <p>Students have multiple opportunities to connect and share ideas, hobbies and interests on and off campus. Social events are organised throughout the year, including sports tournaments, cultural shows, academic competitions, and more. Multiple student clubs allow individuals to meet like-minded students who share their interests and celebrate different cultures.</p>",
